It looks like a tie clasp.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, isn't that really -
That's top-level.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.673 size:88% position:44%
-I was thinking like --
That looks pretty sharp.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What do you guys wear?
Is that what you do at CNN

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, just this.
-It's like that?

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:13.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yours looks cool,
like it's intended.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:13.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you have
your own show, too.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.349 line:92%
You've got to get one of these

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't have as much pull
I don't think.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Well, the problem is,
you have a show

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a network
that has too many hosts.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:25.425
So they'd be like, "You get one,
then Cuomo's going to want one

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anderson's going to want one."
-Exactly.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can't do that.
Whereas me, it's --

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not just one tie clip.
-I guarantee you,

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
if I've got it,
that means Fallon had it first

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:34.768 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It does actually
have his initials.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.838 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It does, yeah.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:42.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"J.F. -- do not touch."
Oh, no.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You hosted the debates.
-I did.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And that is a lot.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not only was it
back-to-back nights,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.748 line:92%
but 10 candidates both nights.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you -- How do you approach
it with that many people?

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:54.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, first of all,
we should just make sure
everybody understands.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:58.224
If it were up to me, I would
have like five candidates.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it was the Democratic
National Committee.

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.295
They made the decision.
-Right. Not CNN's choice.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.998 size:88% position:44%
-And they said, "This is
what you have to achieve

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
in order to get on
the debate stage."

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it turns out
it was very achievable.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So they had 20 candidates

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank God we were allowed
to split it into two nights.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:17.677
And it's tough, because al
these competing imperatives.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:20.947
You want to make sure that
you get to the big people,

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:24.584
the bigger candidates, but you
also want to include everybody

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:25.785 line:92%
You want to bring out debate

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:27.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to get to as many
topics as you can,

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you don't want
to be too shallow.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
it's a lot of moving parts

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.193 line:92%
-It did seem that you guys

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:36.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
got credit for hitting on
a lot of substantive issues.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:37.664 line:92%
Obviously, a limit of time

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the fact that 10 peopl
are talking.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think when --
We remember the last debat

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:46.106
that had that many candidate
was the GOP debates 4 years ago.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:46.973 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You did those, as well.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yea, I did one
with 11 candidates.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:50.910 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-11 candidates at once.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because Carly Fiorina
got in there.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.013
-She slid in at the last minute.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And thank God she did,
because then she was president

00:01:57.016 --> 00:02:00.386
But you -- Those, I think,
are not remembered as bein

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:04.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
as substantive, but you woul
argue that they were.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.792 line:92%
We just forget because of Trump.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because of who was
in the middle of the stage

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.730
I think we asked a lot
of substantive questions,

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think one of the problem
with a debate

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:16.302
anytime that President Trump -
then candidate Trump -- is there

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
is, you might not remember
the discussion

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:23.076
about the nuclear triad, for
example, which was brought up.

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:27.080
And you might remember whe
he made fun of Rand Paul's hair.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-One of them might stick out -

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
stick in your brain
a little bit more.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.287
-Yeah. Do you think that wil
ultimately be the challeng

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:37.490
for whoever ends up against him,
moving forward?

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that -- As voters,
we will also be distracted

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:44.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
by his ability to make fun o
sort of trivial things?

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know. That's going to
be the big challenge

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
for whoever
the Democratic nominee is.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.370 line:92%
What's the way to go after him

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.204 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Because you could argue

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Hillary Clinton won
all three debates.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.842 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, I think pretty --
Like, by a clear margin.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:59.045
-Polls indicated that the
American people thought she did.

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And then, yet,

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's obviously not
at the White House right now

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, 'cause they were like
"That other guy

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a little crazy, though.
I kind of like that.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:08.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's see what that looks like
in the White House.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:09.923 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Let's try the crazy guy.

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:13.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's only for a week, right?
Four years?!"

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.262
-It was a little bit more
complicated than that.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.198 line:92%
But okay. We'll go with that

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think most voters --
Trust me.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:22.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been in the diners.
That's what they did.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.804
I've talked to people in diners.
So you --

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:28.141 size:88% position:44%
-There were the Russians
and Comey and Wisconsin.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's a lot of things.
-A lot of factors.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:33.746
-You've had this issue,
because you have to deal with it

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:36.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
certainly in a more serious wa
than we do.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:37.584 line:92%
There have been things this week

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:41.054 size:88% position:44%
that are hard to lay out
exactly what happened.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:44.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
Steve King,
who is an Iowa Congressman

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:47.994
he basically made comments
defending rape and incest.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:51.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which you would think
would be a real career ender

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.966 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but not as yet.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you even --
When you hear that,

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.070
how do you even go about
presenting that to people

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
as "here's a real thing
that happened"?

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I mean,
we just ran the clip.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:04.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just for those of you
who are not familiar

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:07.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
With Congressman King's
oeuvre...

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:07.847 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:07.847 --> 00:04:12.819
-He says a lot of just reall
insane and offensive things.

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.287 line:92%
-Yeah, the craziest thing is

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:16.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
it wasn't out of left fiel
for him.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:19.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. The good news was,
it wasn't racist.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.494 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, that's right.
He tried a new thing.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's like,
be careful what you wish for

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.932 size:88% position:44%
It's like -- Good news.
He's not racist anymore.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it wasn't that --
Just in those comments he was,

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm going to try
a little misogyny.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's just see how that goes
Try it on for size."

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, the basic argument
he was making,

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was trying to explain -
he was trying to defend

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:39.412 size:81% position:41%
his argument as to why
he does not support --

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:40.813 size:88% position:44% line:92%
he's opposed to abortion

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:45.785
and he does not even believe i
exemptions for rape and incest

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:48.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
And his argument was,
"If you go back in history

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
a lot of people got raped

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:52.225 line:92%
and a lot of people had incest

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:54.894
and I don't know that my famil
tree doesn't have any of that.

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:59.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I'd argue
it probably does, yeah.

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.700 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.069 size:88% position:44%
-It would explain a lot.
-Yeah. It would, yeah.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, anyway,
so, in that instance,

00:05:06.172 --> 00:05:07.006 size:78% position:39% line:92%
we just ran the clip.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.509 size:81% position:41%
And then I just turned
to a guy on the panel,

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
poor Mike Rogers,
former Republican Congressman,

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just said, "Why does he sa
things like that?"

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:20.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-He didn't have an answer.

